@startuml
title The render ledger — the life of one entry: dispatch owes a page

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #0b7a75
skinparam StateBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam StateBackgroundColor #fdfdfd
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9ca3af

[*] --> Expected : navigator dispatches;\nrecords the expectation

state Expected #fdfdfd
state "Closed" as Closed #eef6f5
state "Timed out" as TimedOut #f9efef
state Responded #fdfdfd

Expected --> Closed : internal_callback arrives,\nour_signature verified
Expected --> TimedOut : a timeout fact wins\nthe race (render /\ncallback / external_call)

Closed --> Responded : merged (serial, deterministic);\na conflict is an exception
TimedOut --> Responded : the navigator answers\nwhether or not the page rendered

Responded --> [*]

note right of Expected
  One entry per dispatched piece of work.
  The completion callback closes it, or a
  configurable timeout fact closes it first —
  whichever wins the race.
end note

note right of TimedOut
  A governance timeout is fatal.
  A user-facing timeout explains, in
  layman's terms, what timed out and,
  where useful, asks the person to retry.
end note

note bottom of Responded
  A page is complete when its entries are.
  The navigator holds the ledger; a satellite's
  tools answer through the proxy as callbacks.
end note
@enduml
